From: Mehmet Salih <salihmehmet497@gmail.com>
Subject: ARM: airoha: link the kernel 0x88000 into DRAM to keep clear of ATF

On EN7523 boards the vendor boot chain (BL2 -> BL32/sp_min -> U-Boot) leaves
the AArch32 Trusted Firmware runtime resident at the very start of DRAM
(vendor DT: atf-reserved-memory@80000000, 0x40000 bytes, no-map). With the
default TEXT_OFFSET of 0x8000 the raw kernel Image lands at 0x80008000 and
overwrites it, so the first PSCI SMC ("psci: probing for conduit method
from DT") jumps into kernel text and the boot locks up hard -- which is
exactly what was observed on the Zyxel EX3501-T0 and mis-diagnosed as
"this U-Boot has no PSCI conduit". The vendor kernel is linked at
PAGE_OFFSET + 0x88000 (virt 0xC0088000, phys 0x80088000) for this reason.

Use the same text offset for ARCH_AIROHA so head.S still derives
PHYS_OFFSET = 0x80000000 from the 0x80088000 load address, and the EL3
runtime survives. Pair with KERNEL_LOADADDR := 0x80088000 in the image
recipe and re-enable the psci node / cpu enable-method in the board DT.

--- a/arch/arm/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/Makefile
@@ -160,6 +160,8 @@
 # during boot, and this offset is critical to the functioning of
 # kexec-tools.
 textofs-y	:= 0x00008000
+# Airoha EN7523: keep the kernel above the resident AArch32 TF-A (sp_min)
+textofs-$(CONFIG_ARCH_AIROHA) := 0x00088000
 # RTD1195 has Boot ROM at start of address space
 textofs-$(CONFIG_ARCH_REALTEK)  := 0x00108000
 # SA1111 DMA bug: we don't want the kernel to live in precious DMA-able memory
